Patch: 0001-sequence-random-arguments.patch
Applies to: native/vendor/dungeonmaker-2.05/DungeonMaker.cpp
What: Draws random values that were passed as several function arguments of one call
  (five Mutate2() genes per random Crawler in Init_fromConfig, x/y of the start square
  in PlonkDownStuff) into local variables first, in parameter order (left to right).
Why: C++ leaves the evaluation order of function arguments unspecified (GCC on x86-64
  evaluates right to left, clang/Emscripten left to right), so the same seed produced
  different dungeons per compiler for every design with random Crawlers (K record).
  Spec section 5.3 promises identical output on every platform.
Date: 2026-10-31
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

